  "observations": {
    "original_input": "The first client sent F8 and timed out before receiving it. Its frame 0 screen pixels were correct. A DWM OpenResource event occurred before WindowsBegin.",
    "corrected_input": "The only client changes established source keyboard focus, populated the scan code, and waited for both real key messages. Two distinct RGB patterns matched in the source window and its mirror.",
    "target_import": "Neither trace established a Windows-produced standard GDI allocation entering the GM20B production OpenResource handler with allocation-only data. The layered-window test passed. The import candidate remains unqualified.",
    "other_coverage": "Earlier same-adapter production texture control carried 72 resource-private bytes. The WARP allocation-only texture was rejected on crossing adapters.",
    "present1": "The process-level Present1 candidate was outside these cases."
  },
